xnu 0424: the WLAN country as Apple's driver handles it: wifid's COUNTRY_CODE applied, channels from the rules

wifid asks for COUNTRY_CODE (Apple80211 51) and the kernel refused it, so the WLAN firmware kept the board data's own
regdomain and iOS a fixed channel list (0123). As Apple's driver (dev-notes/investigacion/anexos/30-wifi/
01-como-lo-hace-apple.md): GET 51 answers {version 1, cc} with the country in force, or XZ when there is none (the
code alone when asked for 3 bytes); SET 51 takes [A-Z]{2} (X* goes back to no country), has the radio apply it,
leaves a network whose channel the country does not allow, sends the new channel list and posts event 11
(APPLE80211_M_COUNTRY_CODE_CHANGED). Every GET/SET 51 is logged (the code only).

The radio applies it the way qcacld-3.0 talks to this firmware family, chosen by what the firmware announces: with
WMI_SERVICE_REGULATORY_DB, SET_CURRENT_COUNTRY with the code and the channels from the firmware's REG_CHAN_LIST_CC
rules; without it, PDEV_SET_REGDOMAIN with qcacld's regdomain/domains/CTL for the country and qcacld's rules for its
channels. Both tables (sapphire_wlan_regdb.h) are generated by tools/wlan-regdb-gen.py from qcacld's cds_regdomain.c
and reg_db.c (sources and sha256 in the header). With no country the channels are those of the board data's own
regdomain (the firmware's first REG_CHAN_LIST_CC, or qcacld's rules for the eeprom_rd that SERVICE_READY reports;
0123's list only if neither exists). Per-channel power and passive/radar marks come from the rules. The country in
force is sent again when the firmware reports WMI READY again. SERVICE_READY's eeprom_rd and hardware tx power are
logged. 0297's -85 dBm auto-join threshold is unchanged (no Apple value found for it).
